    > dential/5%-sample/h1_dataset.dta saved

. 
.         
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * 
. 
.         * We regress  the gender eqiality index (GE_index) [0,1] onto the ind
> icator 
.         * of having at least one daughter in 2018 and a group of control vari
> ables 
.         * that, according to previous findings, have an effect on the gender 
.         * equality attitudes. 
. 
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with GE_index 
> as 
.         * dependent variable and the dummy variable d_daughter and additional
>  
.         * controls as independent variables. We also control for missing valu
> es of 
.         * control variables. 
.         
.         * The coefficient estimate of variable d_daughter is of main interest
> .
.         * We use robust standard errors. 
.         
.         reg GE_index i.d_daughter c.age i.mig i.educ i.east i.female  i.marri
> tal_stat  i.polit i.religiosity, r

